# SATUSEHAT-4B — Structured Diagnosis Adoption & Clinical Terminology Rollout

1. SATUSEHAT-2 remains WATCH; its GO tag remains absent. SATUSEHAT-4B is
   credential-independent: no OAuth/sandbox/production/external FHIR HTTP.
2. Structured diagnosis uses the canonical 4A tables
   (`mst_clinical_diagnoses`, `trx_medical_record_diagnoses`) — never a
   parallel diagnosis subsystem or second data-quality engine.
3. Legacy free text is never auto-coded; no guessed ICD/SNOMED/clinical code;
   no AI auto-coding; no bulk mutation of historical RME.
4. Terminology lifecycle: draft → under_review → approved → active →
   deprecated/rejected. Activation requires an official source + clinical
   review (`review_clinical_terminology`); separation of duties is
   server-side (creator/submitter can never approve their own entry). All
   transitions via `ClinicalDiagnosisService` (row-locked) — never direct
   status writes.
5. Active terminology is immutable; corrections create a new entry and
   deprecate the old one with an ACTIVE replacement pointer. Deprecated codes
   stay historically readable and are only excluded from new selection.
6. Only ACTIVE terminology is selectable for new records (search repository +
   `MedicalRecordDiagnosisService::record` both enforce it). Synthetic
   rehearsal entries are lifecycle-exempt (isolated campaign only).
7. Rollout modes (`disabled|informational|warning|pilot_enforced`) are
   branch-scoped via `DiagnosisRolloutService`/`mst_diagnosis_rollout_settings`
   — resolved server-side from the record's branch, never request input.
   **Global hard enforcement is forbidden by design**: the config default must
   stay non-blocking and is refused otherwise; enforcement is only per-branch,
   reasoned, audited (`configure_diagnosis_rollout`).
8. `pilot_enforced` blocks ONLY `MedicalRecordService::finalize()` and only
   without an ACTIVE-terminology primary diagnosis or a usable override.
   It never bypasses/blocks room, consent, cashier, payment, or visit rules.
9. Emergency override: dedicated `override_diagnosis_requirement` permission +
   MedicalRecordPolicy re-check, reason ≥10 chars, time-boxed, append-only,
   audited — and it NEVER makes the SATUSEHAT candidate ready.
10. Exactly one primary diagnosis per record (service-enforced; the HARD
    `duplicate_primary_diagnosis` rule guards history). Primary swaps only via
    the explicit audited `makePrimary` — never silent.
11. Diagnosis facts hash terminology status + mapping code/system/display +
    role: any post-approval diagnosis/terminology/mapping change drifts the
    source hash and revokes the candidate approval (re-review required).
    Unchanged records must never fabricate drift.
12. Condition preview is built ONLY from structured diagnoses + ACTIVE
    reviewed mappings; unmapped ⇒ `mapping_blocked`; local preview is never
    remote acceptance; NIK never rendered; primary/secondary carried as local
    context (no unverified FHIR rank extension).
13. Adoption analytics (`SatusehatDiagnosisAdoptionService`, dashboard,
    `satusehat:diagnosis-adoption-audit`) are read-only, PII-free,
    RME-branch-scoped (crafted branch ids dropped), null-not-zero rates, and
    are operational quality indicators — never a punitive ranking.
14. HARD diagnosis issues (`duplicate_primary_diagnosis`,
    `diagnosis_code_invalid`) can never be waived into SATUSEHAT-ready status.
15. Production stays blocked (SATUSEHAT-3 guard); no auto-send; no "Send All";
    external GO depends on the SATUSEHAT-2 credential closure campaign.
